{
  "decision": "PROMOTE",
  "why": "Zero 5xx on both versions: every one of the 9819 requests returned 200 (claim 1). The canary's elevated latency is confined to the start of the test: in 0-30s canary p95 was more than 1.5x stable p95, while in the 90-120s window canary p95 matches stable within 5 ms (claim 2). Over the whole steady-state last 60 s, canary p95 is within 5 ms of stable p95 (claim 3), and that parity holds per endpoint for /browse, /search and /checkout (claim 4). The canary carried 25.2% of traffic, n=2476 requests, so the sample is large enough to see a real regression (claim 5). JUDGEMENT: the first-minute p95 elevation that dominates the dashboard's whole-test aggregates (canary p95 177 vs stable 94) is the warm-up signature of one freshly started pod - JIT/code cache, cold caches, connection-pool and DNS fill - because it decays monotonically and then disappears rather than persisting or worsening; a genuine code regression would not heal by itself while load stays constant at 80 req/s. JUDGEMENT: with no errors and steady-state latency at parity, the release risk is low and blocking it is the worse error, so promote. JUDGEMENT: promote gradually (e.g. 25 -> 50 -> 100%) and pre-warm new pods or keep them out of rotation briefly, since each new pod will show the same ~60 s warm-up bump; roll back if steady-state p95 diverges from the 1.0 baseline or any 5xx appear.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "There were no server errors at all: 0 5xx on canary and 0 on stable, and all 9819 logged requests returned HTTP 200.",
      "query": "const c5=canary.filter(r=>r.status>=500).length, s5=stable.filter(r=>r.status>=500).length; print('5xx canary='+c5+' stable='+s5+' total_rows='+rows.length); print('non200='+rows.filter(r=>r.status!==200).length);",
      "expect": "5xx canary=0 stable=0 total_rows=9819"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The canary's latency penalty is an early transient: in 0-30s its p95 is more than 1.5x stable's, but in the final 90-120s window its p95 is within 5 ms of stable's.",
      "query": "const q=(a,p)=>{const x=a.slice().sort((m,n)=>m-n);return x[Math.min(x.length-1,Math.ceil(p*x.length)-1)];}; const w=(a,b,rs)=>rs.filter(r=>r.t>=a&&r.t<b).map(r=>r.ms); const c1=q(w(0,30,canary),0.95), s1=q(w(0,30,stable),0.95), c4=q(w(90,120.1,canary),0.95), s4=q(w(90,120.1,stable),0.95); print('0-30s   p95 canary='+c1+' stable='+s1); print('90-120s p95 canary='+c4+' stable='+s4); print('EARLY_SPIKE='+(c1>1.5*s1)+' LATE_PARITY='+(Math.abs(c4-s4)<=5)); print('WARMUP_SPIKE_EARLY_AND_GONE='+(c1>1.5*s1&&Math.abs(c4-s4)<=5));",
      "expect": "WARMUP_SPIKE_EARLY_AND_GONE=true"
    },
    {
      "claim": "In the steady-state last 60 s of the test, canary p95 is within 5 ms of stable p95.",
      "query": "const q=(a,p)=>{const x=a.slice().sort((m,n)=>m-n);return x[Math.min(x.length-1,Math.ceil(p*x.length)-1)];}; const c=canary.filter(r=>r.t>=60).map(r=>r.ms), s=stable.filter(r=>r.t>=60).map(r=>r.ms); const cp=q(c,0.95), sp=q(s,0.95); print('last60 n canary/stable='+c.length+'/'+s.length); print('last60 p95 canary='+cp+' stable='+sp+' diff='+(cp-sp)); print('last60 p99 canary='+q(c,0.99)+' stable='+q(s,0.99)); print('STEADY_PARITY_WITHIN_5MS='+(Math.abs(cp-sp)<=5));",
      "expect": "STEADY_PARITY_WITHIN_5MS=true"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Steady-state parity holds per endpoint: in the last 60 s, canary p95 for /browse, /search and /checkout is no more than 10 ms above stable's.",
      "query": "const q=(a,p)=>{const x=a.slice().sort((m,n)=>m-n);return x[Math.min(x.length-1,Math.ceil(p*x.length)-1)];}; let ok=true; for(const p of ['/browse','/search','/checkout']){const c=canary.filter(r=>r.t>=60&&r.path===p).map(r=>r.ms), s=stable.filter(r=>r.t>=60&&r.path===p).map(r=>r.ms); const cp=q(c,0.95), sp=q(s,0.95); print(p+' last60 n='+c.length+'/'+s.length+' p95 canary='+cp+' stable='+sp); if(!(cp<=sp+10)) ok=false;} print('ALL_PATHS_STEADY_PARITY='+ok);",
      "expect": "ALL_PATHS_STEADY_PARITY=true"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The canary received 25.2% of the traffic, 2476 of 9819 requests.",
      "query": "print('canary_share='+(canary.length/rows.length*100).toFixed(1)+'% n='+canary.length+'/'+rows.length);",
      "expect": "canary_share=25.2% n=2476/9819"
    }
  ]
}

